13:["$","div",null,{"className":"prose-custom max-w-none","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["# Email Personalization Beyond First Name: Advanced Strategies That Drive Results"]}],["$","p","2",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["> ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Excerpt:"}]," Personalization goes far beyond inserting a first name. This guide covers behavioral targeting, dynamic content blocks, and product recommendations -- backed by real data and actionable tactics you can implement *this week*."]}],["$","p","4",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["For years, marketers have leaned on the \"Hi, [First Name]\" opener as the gold standard of email personalization. But here's the hard truth: ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"using a subscriber's first name alone increases open rates by just 2-5%"}]," (Experian, 2023), and has *zero impact* on conversion or revenue when used in isolation."]}],["$","p","6",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["True personalization isn't about salutations -- it's about relevance at scale. It's delivering the *right message*, to the *right person*, at the *right time*, based on *real behavior*, not assumptions."]}],["$","p","8",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["In this post, we'll move past surface-level tactics and explore three advanced, high-ROI personalization strategies -- each with concrete data, implementation tips, and real-world examples."]}],["$","hr","10",{"className":"border-[#5F1E1E] my-8"}],["$","h2","12",{"className":"text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-10 mb-4 tracking-tight","children":"1. Behavioral Targeting: Trigger Emails That Respond to Actions (Not Just Time)"}],["$","p","14",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["Behavioral targeting means sending emails triggered by *what subscribers actually do*: pages visited, products viewed, cart abandonment, email engagement history, or even time spent reading a blog post."]}],["$","h3","16",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"✅ Why It Works"}],["$","p","17",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["According to Omnisend, ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"behavioral emails generate 3x more transactions and 2.7x higher revenue per email"}]," than batch-and-blast campaigns. More strikingly, ",["$","strong","3",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"abandoned cart emails with personalized product thumbnails see 49% higher click-through rates"}]," (Barilliance, 2024)."]}],["$","h3","19",{"className":"text-lg font-bold text-[#FEF2F0] mt-8 mb-3","children":"🛠 Actionable Steps"}],["$","p","20",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- ",["$","strong","1",{"className":"font-bold text-[#FEF2F0]","children":"Map micro-behaviors to triggers"}],":"]}],["$","p","21",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Viewed product page (but didn't add to cart) → Send \"You might love this\" email with that item + 2 complementary SKUs within 1 hour."]}],["$","p","22",{"className":"text-[#BE8A83] leading-relaxed mb-4 text-base","children":["- Opened last 3 emails but never clicked → Deploy a \"We miss you\" re-engagement sequence with a value-driven offer (e.g., \"Here's what you missed...\" + exclusive content)."]}],"$L17","$L18","$L19","$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d","$L1e","$L1f","$L20","$L21","$L22","$L23","$L24","$L25","$L26","$L27","$L28","$L29","$L2a","$L2b","$L2c","$L2d","$L2e","$L2f","$L30","$L31","$L32","$L33","$L34","$L35","$L36","$L37","$L38","$L39","$L3a","$L3b","$L3c","$L3d","$L3e","$L3f","$L40","$L41","$L42","$L43","$L44","$L45","$L46",